The power-domain action preserves composition. The action of a composite equals the composite of the actions.

In one direction the source neighbourhood is generated by a finite list. Each generator has a composite witness in the target, and those intermediate neighbourhoods are gathered into one list. The union of their up-sets is the intermediate power-domain neighbourhood, and monotonicity of the two maps extends the relations from generators to all members. In the other direction the intermediate neighbourhood supplies the two existential witnesses, which are paired into a witness for the composite.
